package, and any process that reads the package and the claim immediately forms a provisional answer, making itself the author whose search E-B rules inadmissible.\",\n      \"required_evidence\": \"A record of a systematic search over the domain (e.g. structured enumeration of the boundary classes, or exhaustive/bounded enumeration of small interval lists) produced by a process that is not the author of the provisional verdict; on a HOLDS outcome, that party's argument that no violating input exists in the domain.\",\n      \"admissibility_constraints\": [\n        \"Task requirement E-B: the search must be 'carried out by a party other than the author of the provisional answer, or such a party's argument that no violating input exists in the domain'.\",\n        \"The searching party must therefore be a separately launched process: either one that sees the provisional answer but did not author it, or one causally isolated from the worker's conclusions that searches unanchored.\",\n        \"The search record must survive its originating session and be integrated into the deliverable by the governed root step to count.\"\n      ],\n      \"evidence_requirement_refs\": [\n        \"E-B\"\n      ],\n      \"dependencies\": [\n        \"Q1\"\n      ],\n      \"features\": {\n        \"locally_resolvable\": false,\n        \"requires_isolation\": true,\n        \"contamination\": true,\n        \"capability_bearing_artifact\": false,\n        \"spans_sessions\": true\n      }\n    }\n  ]\n}\n","numLines":76,"startLine":1,"totalLines":76}}}
